{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381719-vampire-20th-question-magic-resistance","id":1381719,"title":"Vampire 20th Question: Magic Resistance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-15T11:43:09-07:00","id":1381719,"title":"Vampire 20th Question: Magic Resistance","content":"The Magic Resistance Merit states that &quot;You maynever learn magical Disciplines such as Thaumaturgy and Necromancy&quot;. Which Disciplines are actually barred due to this Merit? I assume any form of blood magic, such as Wanga, Koldunic Sorcery, and the like is right out. I remember one Revised book, Blood Treachery, which claimed some Disciplines were 'magical', such as Quietus and I think Chimerstry. Would these Discipines be affected by Magic Resistance? And what about Abyssal Mysticism- would a Magic Resistance character be unable to learn Abyssal Rituals, or even Obtenebration itself? I'm also curious about Sabbat Rites, which are also stated to be a magical investment, and &quot;Dark&quot; Thaumaturgy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T04:47:58-07:00","id":1381892,"title":"","content":"I would say you are barred from all the Blood Sorceries:<br /> Tremere Thaumaturgy, Necromancy, Koldunic Sorcery (and Kraina), Dur'An'Ki, all kinds of Setite Sorcery (Akhu, Wanga, Nahualotl, Sadhana), Abyss mysticism, the Anarch Sorceries, the Inconnu Thaumaturgies... and probably a few niche ones I missed.<br /> <br /> Dark Thaumaturgy is a harder nut to crack, but I also have massive bleeding soft spot for infernals and all their fun shenanigans. I would maybe say that you need some fuel source besides blood to perform your magics, like sacrifices to your demon master.<br /> <br /> I would not ban any &quot;natural&quot; disciplines that Vampires develop with time and bloodlust, like Celerity, Dominate, Chimerstry or Viscissitude (viscissitude is a discipline, not an alien brain parasite, fight me).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Furthermore, I believe Carthage should be destroyed.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23835-pang4","name":"pang4","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T14:18:15-07:00","id":1381976,"title":"","content":"Oh another one that I'm unsure about. Flight, since it even says some magic use shows in the Gargoyle's aura when in use. A case could be made for Visceratika itself, I suppose, given it's origins. Also, is Abyss Mysticism really blood Sorcery? It's such a weird (but not unique) concept, rituals that key off of a non-Sorcerous Discipline (not unique because there's mention of a Temporis ritual to preserve books). I mean, what's next, a Discipline you can catch like a disease? Oh...wait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T00:22:14-07:00","id":1382464,"title":"","content":"I think Dark Thaumaturgy and Daimonion could be potential exceptions to the ban, as they're being granted/fueled by otherworldly powers rather than just developed through time, research, and experimentation with the power in one's own blood. Though at least for the former, how one gets in contact with the otherworldly forces without being able to perform magic in the first place is the $64,000 question. I could see Abyss Mysticism going either way, but I really don't think it's an appropriate Merit to choose for a character who is or will become an Abyss mystic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T12:20:49-07:00","id":1382570,"title":"","content":"<i>Potence </i>is magical. You think you can put your fist through a wall using just normal physical strength? The only 'Magical' disciplines in the context of this merit are the ones that require belief systems to operate <i>and </i>Have a system of paths and rituals. Quietus doesn't need the former, Chimestry doesn't have the latter. Obtenebration needs neither to function at a basic level and is very limited at a higher level (The most advanced obtenebration belief system doesn't compare to what's basically needed to get magic working) <br /> <br /> Explicitly, you can't use thaumaturgy or necromancy. Assamite Dur-An-ki, Settite Akhu, Punk sorcery and a whole load of other things are just Thaumaturgy with a different paradigm. You'll note they have the same powers and call them different things. <br /> <br /> Koldunic sorcery has &quot;Sorcery&quot; in the name. I think we can put that safely in the &quot;no&quot; pile. <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, where the fun begins. <br /> Abyss mysticism... I'd say it works. You're not<i> learning</i> a magical discipline, you're doing things with a normal (albiet mystical) discipline. The rules lawyer and the lore enthusiast within me both say it's fine. <br /> <br /> Dark thaumaturgy wise.<br /> I believe a demon could remove this &quot;merit&quot;, and could then bestow power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T13:07:05-07:00","id":1382579,"title":"","content":"DAV20's definition of &quot;blood sorcery&quot; is anything that gets you Paths and/or Rituals. So Quietus isn't affected, Sabbat Ritae aren't affected, Obtenebration isn't affected, Abyss Mysticism is, Dark Thaumaturgy is. (Though, as MyWifeIsScary said, an infernal pact could potentially just remove the Magic Resistance before giving you Dark Thaum.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T15:56:47-07:00","id":1382625,"title":"","content":"Most of these questions are academic, since the only real answer is &quot;ask your Storyteller&quot;, but I appreciate the answers. I don't know offhand if it's still true, but in Revised, a character with Magic Resistance COULD learn Thaumaturgy, in the form of Countermagic, though at that point, the question of whether Countermagic is it's own Discipline that functions identically to Perdo Magica manifests. IF infernal sorcery is learnable by even the magic resistant, I'd be curious to hear why Koldunic Sorcery would be banned; it is, after all, granted by &quot;demons&quot;. I'm still iffy about Rites, given their ties to Koldunism. Ritual uses of Disciplines like Abyssal Mysticism, or the theoretical Temporis ritual I don't have a good answer for, one way or the other. Most of this discussion spawned from a sidebar in Blood Treachery that discusses what Disciplines can be countered by Mages (and, I assume, resisted by the armor of HIT Mark V's).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T03:19:38-07:00","id":1383114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lynceus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381719-vampire-20th-question-magic-resistance?p=1382625#post1382625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of these questions are academic,.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being a wizard to some extent requires you to be an academic. Even chaos sorcerers got to know a lot of things to get the intuition going. <br /> <br /> Koldunic sorcery was allegedly sourced from the teachings of a demon. It's not granted to people via infernal investment, it's just taught. <br /> As for DT, the reason why I think it's ok is not because it's ok, but because demons can make changes to individiuals and remove the merit of magic resistance, allowing the person to learn normally or recieve DT. <br /> <br /> For Abyss mysticism<br /> I believe Thaumaturgy and disciplines like it essentially opperate with a system of bottlenecks. You can't learn a path or ritual that exceeds your discipline rating, You can gain the knowledge on how to use them, but you aren't able to practice them. Once you've pushed your discipline rating beyond the required level of rituals, you can learn anything you like, given time and study. With abyss mysticism, the discipline itself is not impeded by any magic-incapable merits/flaws, so you should be able to use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T11:10:42-07:00","id":1383169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381719-vampire-20th-question-magic-resistance?p=1383114#post1383114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Abyss mysticism<br /> I believe Thaumaturgy and disciplines like it essentially opperate with a system of bottlenecks. You can't learn a path or ritual that exceeds your discipline rating, You can gain the knowledge on how to use them, but you aren't able to practice them. Once you've pushed your discipline rating beyond the required level of rituals, you can learn anything you like, given time and study. With abyss mysticism, the discipline itself is not impeded by any magic-incapable merits/flaws, so you should be able to use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, interesting. So you're saying anyone can learn Thaumaturgical rituals, because they're just a series of instructions anyone can follow, you just can't make them work without the discipline of Thaumaturgy, and Magic Resistance blocks you from getting that discipline?<br /> <br /> I could see an argument being made for that; in that case, I'd also expect people with Magic Resistance to be able to do gutter-magic/hedge-magic. Does the merit itself say anything about that? (I don't have my V20 core with me rn)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T13:58:35-07:00","id":1383210,"title":"","content":"WARNING: very long post!<br /> <br /> Magic Resistance: You have an inherent resistance to the rituals of the Tremere and the spells of the mages of other Clans. The difficulty of all such magic, both malicious and beneficent, is two higher when directed at you. You may never learn magical Disciplines such as Thaumaturgy<br /> and Necromancy.<br /> <br /> It appears this version of the Merit doesn't mention non-Kindred magic, and it uses the most common forms of Blood Magic as it's examples. So maybe it only works against Blood Magic? That could be rough in a crossover game, but those are already bothersome. Imagine trying to figure out if it worked against Gifts or Changeling Arts. There seems to be some inconsistencies with Thaumaturgical Countermagic, which states the following:<br /> <br /> &quot;This is less of a path than it is a separate Discipline, as the power to resist Thaumaturgy can be taught independently of Thaumaturgy, even to those Kindred who are incapable of mastering the simplest ritual.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Thaumaturgical Countermagic can be learned by characters who are unable to learn Thaumaturgy (e.g., those with the Merit Magic Resistance).&quot;<br /> <br /> But then it also says: &quot;Thaumaturgical Countermagic is treated as a separate Discipline, although it uses the the usual rules for Thaumaturgy (including experience costs and the fact that it is limited to only five levels). It cannot be taken as a character's primary path, and a rating in it does not allow the character to perform rituals.&quot;<br /> <br /> So. You can learn Thaumaturgical Countermagic if you have Magic Resistance. BUT it's a path, and it cannot be taken as the primary path. And someone with Magic Resistance can't learn Thaumaturgy. Kind of wondering how that works...<br /> <br /> Actually, looking at Countermagic, I note that it only has full effectiveness against specifically Thaumaturgy, only works at half strength against other Blood Magic, and has no effect at all against non-Kindred magic. Which is almost an argument reinforcing the idea that Magic Resistance doesn't affect non-Kindred magic, except...<br /> <br /> Page 382 of V20 states: &quot;A vampire with Thaumaturgy or Thaumaturgical<br /> Countermagic can try to counter a magickal spell directed at her; a Wits + Occult roll (difficulty 6) \u201csoaks\u201d such spells, reducing the attack\u2019s potency by one level (or die) per success. A vampire who eliminates a mage\u2019s successes neutralizes the wizard\u2019s spell. A magi can<br /> also turn this ability around on vampires as well, using their countermagic against Kindred Disciplines.&quot;<br /> <br /> So Countermagic doesn't work against mage powers (except that it does, though admittedly in a non-standard way). Yay!<br /> <br /> But then it also states that Mages can use THEIR countermagic against Kindred Disciplines (and it doesn't specify only &quot;magical&quot; Disciplines). Mind you, these are the V20 rules for Mages, which have their abilities expressed in Vampire rules, as Disciplines themselves.<br /> <br /> All that aside, it seems that Magic Resistance only works against Kindred blood magic. So Akhu, Dur-An-Ki, Thaumaturgy, Necromancy, etc. etc.. It probably works against Dark Thaumaturgy, unless that power is available to creatures without blood to fuel it. It MIGHT work against Obtenebration (which would make Obtenebration susceptible to Countermagic), but it could be that ritual uses of non-Blood Magic Disciplines are exempt. I really think I understand why 5th Edition's version of Obtenebration is explicitly Blood Magic now (and ate Necromancy while it was at it).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24241-lynceus","name":"Lynceus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24241_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T14:28:24-07:00","id":1383222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lynceus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381719-vampire-20th-question-magic-resistance?p=1383210#post1383210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 382 of V20 states: &quot;A vampire with Thaumaturgy or Thaumaturgical<br /> Countermagic can try to counter a magickal spell directed at her; a Wits + Occult roll (difficulty 6) \u201csoaks\u201d such spells, reducing the attack\u2019s potency by one level (or die) per success. A vampire who eliminates a mage\u2019s successes neutralizes the wizard\u2019s spell. A magi can<br /> also turn this ability around on vampires as well, using their countermagic against Kindred Disciplines.&quot;<br /> <br /> So Countermagic doesn't work against mage powers (except that it does, though admittedly in a non-standard way). Yay!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of those rare instances where I much prefer the system from Revised over the one V20 put forth. It used the actual dots in Thaumaturgy as the dice pool against mage powers (+ dots in Thaumaturgical Countermagic, if any), rolled against a difficulty of the mage's Willpower, and every <i>two</i> successes negated one success on the magickal effect. This avoided things like a neonate with one dot in Thaumaturgy, Occult 3, and Wits 5 being able to disrupt magickal effects more easily than an archmage. Members of the Council of Seven or Baba Yaga might be able to roll as many as 14 dice, but functionally they'd be about as effective as a mage with Arete 7.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T06:26:51-07:00","id":1399584,"title":"","content":"to counter that 'obtenebration is now necromancy so it's magical. you should also remember quietus was explicitly not sorcery before v5, and thus the changes of v5 should not influence a game of vtm. <br /> <br /> @Matt<br /> that makes it very harsh to deal with low level magic(k) conflicts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}